      "subject": "bgp",
      "stage": "bgp_fsm",
      "description": "To allow local policy changes to have the correct effect without resetting any BGP connections, a BGP speaker SHOULD either (a) retain the current version of the routes advertised to it by all of its peers for the duration of the connection, or (b) make use of the Route Refresh extension [RFC2918].",
      "is_inferred": false,
      "confidence": 1.0,
